Source: asys
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Roman <roman@nekko.ai>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-python, python3, golang-1.25-go | golang-go (>= 2:1.25~),
 pkg-config, libxaw7-dev, libxmu-dev, libxt-dev, libxft-dev, libxrender-dev, libfontconfig-dev, libx11-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/glguida/asys
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: asys
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10), dcomp (>= 0.3.2),
 asys-images (>= ${source:Upstream-Version}), asys-images (<< ${source:Upstream-Version}+),
 docker.io | docker-ce
Recommends: git, docker-buildx | docker-buildx-plugin
Suggests: asys-flow-view
Description: agent execution environment with logged runs and shared inference
 asys runs LLM agents, goals, BPMN/YAML workflows, programs and human requests
 in Docker environments through dcomp, recording every job. This package
 installs the host commands (asys, asys-run, asys-workers, asys-environment,
 asys-inference, asys-human-prompt), the bundled operating and authoring
 skills, dashboard designs, system agents and examples. The matching
 container images and release record come from asys-images.

Package: asys-flow-view
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: asys (= ${binary:Version})
Description: X11 workflow viewer and editor for asys
 asys-flow-view draws asys workflow files as a map, edits them, follows runs
 and starts them. It talks to "asys workflow serve" and needs only the
 libraries every X11 system has (Xt, Xaw, Xmu, Xft, XRender, fontconfig).

Package: asys-server
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, asys (>= ${source:Version}), adduser, python3
Recommends: nginx
Description: shared team deployment of asys under /srv/asys
 Creates the asys group and service user, initializes group-shared asys
 state under /srv/asys/host (dcomp state inside it, as upstream documents),
 runs the dashboard as a system service, and provides asys-adduser,
 asys-skills and asys-server-update helpers. On upgrade it refreshes
 running shared services with "asys update" when no run is active.
